#: C:\Users\tamas\Studio\plugin23456\wp-content\plugins\refitune\admin\page-help.php
msgid ""
"Adds role-based controls to the shared <strong>Visibility</strong> panel on every "
"Gutenberg block, and to the core Hide block modal (Ctrl/Cmd+Shift+H). You can show "
"a block to everyone, to guests only, to any logged-in user, or only to selected "
"WordPress roles.<br><br><strong>How it works:</strong> matching happens server-side, "
"so non-matching visitors do not receive the block HTML at all.<br><br>"
"<strong>Shared panel:</strong> when Block Visibility (Mobile) is also enabled, "
"device and role controls appear together in the same Visibility panel / Hide modal."
"<br><br><strong>Cache warning:</strong> full-page caches that serve the same HTML "
"to guests and logged-in users can show the wrong variant. Separate cache for "
"logged-in traffic (or bypass cache when logged in).<br><br><strong>Note:</strong> "
"do not use this feature as an access-control or secrecy boundary. It omits markup "
"on the front end; it does not encrypt content or protect private data."
msgstr ""

